Inter-Annotator Agreement Report
ShopSmart Advisor, AI6127 | Evaluation set: 1,000 Amazon Electronics review chunks | Task: 3-way polarity (positive / neutral / negative)
1. Setup
Two annotators labeled all 1,000 records independently, using the guideline in the annotation package (subjectivity first, then polarity). Disagreements were adjudicated into a single final label (58 resolved to annotator 1, 48 to annotator 2). [Fill in: who annotator 1 and annotator 2 are, and whether either used LLM assistance. The master file carries an llm_confidence column, so any LLM-drafted labels must be stated here.]
2. Overall agreement
Metric	Value	95% bootstrap CI
Raw agreement	89.4% (894 / 1,000)	87.5% - 91.2%
Cohen's kappa	0.798	0.763 - 0.831
Linearly weighted kappa	0.829	n/a
Raw agreement exceeds the 80% target. By the Landis and Koch scale, kappa of 0.61-0.80 is 'substantial' agreement; 0.798 is at the top of that band.
